Crime and Punishment	1917	{"Derwent Hall Caine","Lydia Knott"}	{"Crime","Drama","Silent"}	Crime and Punishment is a 1917 American silent crime drama film directed by Lawrence B. McGill and starring Derwent Hall Caine, Cherrie Coleman and Lydia Knott. Based on Fyodor Dostoevsky's 1866 novel of the same title, it shifts the setting to portray the protagonist as a Russian immigrant in America.
