The Law of Compensation	1917	{"Norma Talmadge","Fred Esmelton","Chester Barnett"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Law of Compensation is 1917 American silent drama film based on a story by Wilson Mizner and directed by Joseph A. Golden. The film starred Norma Talmadge, who played a dual role, Fred Esmelton, and Chester Barnett. It was produced by Joseph Schenck, the husband of its star Talmadge.
