The Little Yank	1917	{"Dorothy Gish","Frank Bennett"}	{"Historical","Drama","Silent"}	The Little Yank is a 1917 American silent historical drama film directed by George Siegmann and starring Dorothy Gish, Frank Bennett and Bob Burns. The film is set in Kentucky during the American Civil War.
The Lone Wolf	1917	{"Bert Lytell","Hazel Dawn"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Lone Wolf is a 1917 American silent drama film based on the 1914 novel The Lone Wolf by Louis Joseph Vance. Starring Bert Lytell and Hazel Dawn, it was adapted for the screen by George Edwardes-Hall and produced and directed by Herbert Brenon. No prints of the film are known to survive, so it is currently classified as lost.
