The Man Without a Country	1917	{"Florence La Badie","Holmes Herbert"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Man Without a Country is a 1917 American silent film adaptation of Edward Everett Hale's short story The Man Without a Country. It was directed by Ernest C. Warde, and starred Florence La Badie, Holmes Herbert, and J. H. Gilmour, and released by Thanhouser Film Corporation.
