A Modern Musketeer	1917	{"Douglas Fairbanks","Marjorie Daw"}	{"Adventure","Comedy","Silent"}	A Modern Musketeer is a 1917 American silent adventure comedy film directed and written by Allan Dwan. Based on the short story, "D'Artagnan of Kansas" by E. P. Lyle, Jr., the film was produced by and stars Douglas Fairbanks. A now complete and restored print of the film still exists and is currently in the public domain.
