Wee Lady Betty	1917	{"Bessie Love","Frank Borzage","Charles K. French"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Wee Lady Betty is a 1917 American silent drama film produced and distributed by the Triangle Film Corporation. It was directed by Charles Miller and stars Bessie Love, Frank Borzage, and Charles K. French. It is considered lost.
