The Floor Below	1918	{"Mabel Normand","Tom Moore"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	The Floor Below is an American silent film starring Mabel Normand, Tom Moore and Helen Dahl. It was long thought lost, until a print was found "in the estate of a Dutch collector" by the Nederlands Filmmuseum.
Flower of the Dusk	1918	{"Viola Dana","Howard Hall"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Flower of the Dusk is a surviving 1918 silent film directed by John H. Collins and starring his wife Viola Dana. It was produced by Maxwell Karger and distributed by Metro Pictures. The film is based on the 1908 novel by Myrtle Reed.
For Freedom	1918	{"William Farnum","Coit Albertson","Rubye De Remer"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	For Freedom is a 1918 American silent drama film directed by Frank Lloyd and starring William Farnum, Coit Albertson, and Rubye De Remer.
For the Freedom of the East	1918	{"Robert Elliott","Lady Tsen Mei"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	For the Freedom of the East is a lost 1918 silent film drama directed by Ira M. Lowry and starring Lady Tsen Mei. It was produced by Betzwood Pictures, an organization distantly affiliated with the soon to be defunct Lubin Manufacturing Company and distributed by Goldwyn Pictures.
For Husbands Only	1918	{"Mildred Harris","Lew Cody","Kathleen Kirkham"}	{"Comedy","Drama","Silent"}	For Husband's Only is 1918 American silent comedy-drama film and directed by Lois Weber and her husband Phillips Smalley. The film was distributed by Universal Pictures. The film was apparently made in late 1917 but not released until just before the end of World War I. For Husband's Only is now considered to be a lost film.
