Little Miss Hoover	1918	{"Marguerite Clark","Eugene O'Brien","Alfred Hickman"}	{"Romance","Drama","Silent"}	Little Miss Hoover is a 1918 American silent romantic drama film directed by John S. Robertson and stars Marguerite Clark. The film is based on the novel The Golden Bird, by Maria Thompson Daviess. A 35mm print of the film is preserved at the Library of Congress.
