Little Orphant Annie	1918	{"Colleen Moore","Tom Santschi","Harry Lonsdale"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Little Orphant Annie is a 1918 American silent drama film directed by Colin Campbell and stars Colleen Moore, in her first leading role, as the title character. The film is based on James Whitcomb Riley's popular 1885 poem of the same title. Riley also appears in the film.
