Love Me	1918	{"Dorothy Dalton","Jack Holt","William Conklin"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Love Me is a surviving 1918 American drama silent film directed by Roy William Neill and written by C. Gardner Sullivan. The film stars Dorothy Dalton, Jack Holt, William Conklin, Dorcas Matthews, Melbourne MacDowell and Elinor Hancock. The film was released on March 18, 1918, by Paramount Pictures.
