Fighting Cressy	1919	{"Blanche Sweet","Russell Simpson"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Fighting Cressy is a lost 1919 silent film western directed by Robert Thornby and starring Blanche Sweet. It was produced by Jesse D. Hampton and distributed through Pathé Exchange.
The Final Close-Up	1919	{"Shirley Mason","Francis McDonald"}	{"Drama","Silent","War"}	The Final Close-Up is a 1919 American silent drama film directed by Walter Edwards and written by Royal Brown and Julia Crawford Ivers. The film stars Shirley Mason, Francis McDonald, James Gordon, Betty Bouton, Eugene Burr, and Mary Warren. The film was released on May 18, 1919, by Paramount Pictures. It is not known whether the film currently survives.
Fires of Faith	1919	{"Catherine Calvert","Eugene O'Brien","Rubye De Remer"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Fires of Faith is a 1919 American silent drama film directed by Edward José and written by Beulah Marie Dix and Charles E. Whittaker. The film stars Catherine Calvert, Eugene O'Brien, Rubye De Remer, Helen Dunbar, Theodore Roberts, Charles Ogle, and Clarence Geldart. The film with a plot concerning The Salvation Army and World War I was released on August 3, 1919, by Paramount Pictures.
The Firing Line	1919	{"Irene Castle","Isabel West","Vernon Steele"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Firing Line is a lost 1919 American silent drama film directed by Charles Maigne and starring Irene Castle. It was based on the 1908 novel by Robert W. Chambers and produced by Famous Players-Lasky. Paramount Pictures distributed the film.
Flame of the Desert	1919	{"Geraldine Farrar","Lou Tellegen"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Flame of the Desert is a 1919 American silent drama film starring Geraldine Farrar and Lou Tellegen. It was directed by Reginald Barker and produced by Samuel Goldwyn.
Fools and Their Money	1919	{"Emmy Wehlen","Jack Mulhall"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Fools and Their Money is a lost 1919 silent film comedy directed by Herbert Blaché and starring Emmy Wehlen. Maxwell Karger produced and it was released through Metro Pictures.
For a Woman's Honor	1919	{"H. B. Warner","Marguerite De La Motte","John Gilbert"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	For a Woman's Honor is a lost 1919 silent film drama directed by Park Frame. It stars H. B. Warner, a stage actor. John Gilbert has a co-starring role in the feature.
For Better, For Worse	1919	{"Elliott Dexter","Gloria Swanson"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	For Better, for Worse is a 1919 American silent drama film directed by Cecil B. DeMille and starring Gloria Swanson. The film was the second of four "marriage films" directed by DeMille and the second DeMille film starring Gloria Swanson. For Better, for Worse was adapted for the screen by William C. DeMille. Jeanie MacPherson wrote the film's scenario.
Forbidden	1919	{"Mildred Harris","Fred Goodwins"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Forbidden is a lost 1919 American silent drama film directed by Lois Weber and Phillips Smalley and starring Mildred Harris, who was billed as Mrs. Charles Chaplin. The picture was produced and distributed by the Universal Film Manufacturing Company.
The Forfeit	1919	{"House Peters","Hector V. Sarno"}	{"Western","Silent","War"}	The Forfeit is a 1919 American silent Western film directed by Frank Powell and starring House Peters, Jane Miller and William Human.
