Girls	1919	{"Marguerite Clark","Helene Chadwick"}	{"Romance","Comedy","Silent","War"}	Girls is a 1919 American silent romantic comedy directed by Walter Edwards and starring Marguerite Clark. It is based on the 1909 Broadway play of the same name by Clyde Fitch starring Florence Reed in the part Clark plays in this film.
