Her Purchase Price	1919	{"Bessie Barriscale","Alan Roscoe"}	{"Romance","Silent"}	Her Purchase Price is a lost 1919 silent film romance distributed by newly formed Robertson-Cole. It was directed by Howard C. Hickman and starred Bessie Barriscale.
Here Comes the Bride	1919	{"John Barrymore","Frank Losee"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Here Comes the Bride is a lost 1919 American silent comedy film produced by Famous Players-Lasky and released by Paramount Pictures. This film is based on the 1917 Broadway play Here Comes the Bride by Max Marcin and Roy Atwell. The film was directed by John S. Robertson and stars John Barrymore.
His Debt	1919	{"Sessue Hayakawa","Jane Novak"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	His Debt is a 1919 American silent drama film directed by William Worthington and produced by Haworth Pictures Corporation.
His Majesty, the American	1919	{"Douglas Fairbanks","Marjorie Daw"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	His Majesty, the American is a 1919 American silent comedy film directed by Joseph Henabery and starring Douglas Fairbanks. It was the first film produced by United Artists. It was released in the U.K. as One of the Blood. Prints exist in the film holdings of Cohen Media Group [a 35mm positive]; in the film holdings of EmGee Film Library [a 16mm reduction positive]; and in private film collections [a 16mm reduction positives].
His Official Fiancée	1919	{"Vivian Martin","Forrest Stanley","Vera Sisson"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	His Official Fiancée is a lost 1919 American silent comedy film directed by Robert G. Vignola and written by Edith M. Kennedy and Berta Ruck. The film stars Vivian Martin, Forrest Stanley, Vera Sisson, Hugh Huntley, Mollie McConnell, Kathryn Sohn and Tom Ricketts. The film was released on October 16, 1919, by Paramount Pictures.
