In His Brother's Place	1919	{"Hale Hamilton","Marguerite Snow"}	{"Comedy","Drama","Silent"}	In His Brother's Place is a 1919 American silent comedy-drama film, directed by Harry L. Franklin. It stars Hale Hamilton, Emmett C. King, and Ruby Lafayette, and was released on July 14, 1919.
In Honor's Web	1919	{"Harry T. Morey","Agnes Ayres"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	In Honor's Web is a 1919 American silent drama film directed by Paul Scardon, written by Sam Taylor (scenario) and Perry N. Vekroff (story). The film stars Harry T. Morey, Gladden James, and George Backus.
In Mizzoura	1919	{"Noah Beery","Eileen Percy","Monte Blue"}	{"Western","Silent","War"}	In Mizzoura is a lost 1919 American silent Western film starring Robert Warwick and directed by Hugh Ford. This film is based on the 1890s stage play In Mizzoura by Augustus Thomas. The play was previously filmed in 1914.
In Old Kentucky	1919	{"Anita Stewart","Mahlon Hamilton"}	{"Romance","Drama","Silent"}	In Old Kentucky is a 1919 American silent drama film produced by Louis B. Mayer and distributed through First National Attractions, later First National Pictures. The picture was directed by Marshall Neilan and starred Anita Stewart. It was based on the play In Old Kentucky by Charles T. Dazey.
