The Isle of Conquest	1919	{"Norma Talmadge","Wyndham Standing","Charles K. Gerrard"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Isle of Conquest is a 1919 American silent drama film starring Norma Talmadge and produced by Talmadge and her husband Joseph Schenck. The film is now considered lost.
It Pays to Advertise	1919	{"Bryant Washburn","Lois Wilson"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	It Pays to Advertise is a 1919 American silent drama film directed by Donald Crisp and written by Elmer Blaney Harris based upon a play of the same name by Roi Cooper Megrue and Walter C. Hackett. The film stars Bryant Washburn, Lois Wilson, Frank Currier, Walter Hiers, Clarence Geldart, and Julia Faye. The film was released on November 23, 1919, by Paramount Pictures. It is not known whether the film currently survives, and it may be a lost film.
