John Petticoats	1919	{"William S. Hart","Ethel Shannon"}	{"Action","Silent"}	John Petticoats is a 1919 American silent action film directed by Lambert Hillyer and written by C. Gardner Sullivan. The film stars William S. Hart, Walt Whitman, George Webb, Winifred Westover, Ethel Shannon, and Andrew Arbuckle. The film was released on November 2, 1919, by Paramount Pictures.
Johnny Get Your Gun	1919	{"Fred Stone","James Cruze"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Johnny Get Your Gun is a 1919 American comedy silent film directed by Donald Crisp and written by Edmund Lawrence Burke and Gardner Hunting. The film stars Fred Stone, Mary Anderson, Casson Ferguson, James Cruze, Sylvia Ashton, Nina Byron and Mayme Kelso. The film was released on March 16, 1919, by Paramount Pictures.
Johnny-on-the-Spot	1919	{"Hale Hamilton","Louise Lovely","Philo McCullough"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Johnny-on-the-Spot is a 1919 American silent comedy film. Directed by Harry L. Franklin, the film stars Hale Hamilton, Louise Lovely, and Philo McCullough. It was released on February 17, 1919.
Josselyn's Wife	1919	{"Bessie Barriscale","Nigel Barrie"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Josselyn's Wife is a lost 1919 American silent drama film based on a novel by Kathleen Norris. It was directed by Howard C. Hickman and starred Bessie Barriscale, Nigel Barrie, and Joseph J. Dowling. The novel was refilmed again in 1926 with Pauline Frederick.
The Joyous Liar	1919	{"J. Warren Kerrigan","Lillian Walker"}	{"Comedy","Crime","Silent"}	The Joyous Liar is a 1919 American silent comedy film directed by Ernest C. Warde and starring J. Warren Kerrigan, Lillian Walker, and Joseph J. Dowling.
Jubilo	1919	{"Will Rogers","Josie Sedgwick"}	{"Comedy"}	Jubilo is a 1919 American comedy film directed by Clarence G. Badger and written by Robert F. Hill. The film stars Will Rogers, Josie Sedgwick, Charles K. French, Willard Louis, and James Mason. The film was released on December 7, 1919, by Goldwyn Pictures.
