The Probation Wife	1919	{"Norma Talmadge","Thomas Meighan"}	{"Comedy","Drama","Silent"}	The Probation Wife is a 1919 American silent comedy-drama film directed by Sidney Franklin and starring Norma Talmadge. Talmadge served as her own producer with distribution through Select Pictures.
The Profiteers	1919	{"Fannie Ward","Edwin Stevens"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Profiteers is a lost 1919 silent film drama directed by George Fitzmaurice and starring Fannie Ward. It was produced by Astra Films and released through Pathé Exchange.
Prudence on Broadway	1919	{"Olive Thomas","Francis McDonald"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Prudence on Broadway is a lost 1919 American silent comedy film directed by Frank Borzage and starring Olive Thomas. It was produced and distributed by the Triangle Film Corporation.
Puppy Love	1919	{"Lila Lee","Edna Murphy"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Puppy Love is a lost 1919 silent comedy film directed by Roy William Neill with Lila Lee in one of her first starring roles.
Putting It Over	1919	{"Bryant Washburn","Shirley Mason"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Putting It Over is a lost 1919 American silent comedy film directed by Donald Crisp and starring Bryant Washburn. The film was produced by Famous Players-Lasky with distribution being handled by Paramount Pictures.
Putting One Over	1919	{"George Walsh","Matthew Betz"}	{"Drama","Silent","War"}	Putting One Over is a lost 1919 silent film drama directed by Edward Dillon and starring George Walsh. It was produced and directed by Fox Film Corporation.
The Railroader	1919	{"George Fawcett","Virginia True Boardman","Fritzi Brunette"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Railroader is a 1919 American silent drama film directed by Colin Campbell and starring George Fawcett, Virginia True Boardman, and Frank Elliott.
Ravished Armenia	1919	{"Aurora Mardiganian","Irving Cummings"}	{"Drama","Silent","Biography"}	Ravished Armenia, also known as Auction of Souls, is a 1919 American silent film based on the autobiographical book Ravished Armenia by Arshaluys (Aurora) Mardiganian, who also played the lead role in the film. The film, which depicts the 1915 Armenian genocide by the Ottoman Empire from the point of view of Armenian survivor Mardiganian, who plays herself in the film, survives in an incomplete form.
Red Hot Dollars	1919	{"Charles Ray","Gladys George"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Red Hot Dollars is a 1919 American silent drama film directed by Jerome Storm and written by Julien Josephson. The film stars Charles Ray, Gladys George, Charles Hill Mailes, William Conklin, and Mollie McConnell. The film was released on December 28, 1919, by Paramount Pictures. A copy of the film is in the Godfilmofond archive in Moscow.
The Red Lantern	1919	{"Alla Nazimova","Noah Beery"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Red Lantern is a 1919 American silent drama film starring Alla Nazimova, who plays dual roles, and directed by Albert Capellani. It is notable today for being Anna May Wong's screen debut. A single print survives in Europe with rumors of a copy at Gosfilmofond, Moscow.
The Red Viper	1919	{"Gareth Hughes","Ruth Stonehouse","John Gilbert"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Red Viper is a 1919 American silent film drama. It is anti-Communist themed and was produced during the red scare.
The Redhead	1919	{"Alice Brady","Conrad Nagel"}	{"Romance","Drama","Silent"}	Redhead is a lost 1919 American silent drama film directed by Charles Maigne and starring Alice Brady, Conrad Nagel and Robert Schable.
A Regular Girl	1919	{"Elsie Janis","Matt Moore"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	A Regular Girl is a lost 1919 American silent comedy film directed by James Young and starring comedian Elsie Janis. It was produced by Lewis J. Selznick.
The Rescuing Angel	1919	{"Shirley Mason","Forrest Stanley"}	{"Comedy","Silent","War"}	The Rescuing Angel is a 1919 American comedy silent film directed by Walter Edwards and written by Edith Kennedy and Clare Kummer. The film stars Shirley Mason, Forrest Stanley, Arthur Edmund Carewe, John Steppling, Carol Edwards and James Neill. The film was released on April 6, 1919, by Paramount Pictures.
Restless Souls	1919	{"Alma Rubens","Jack Conway"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Restless Souls is a 1919 American silent drama film directed by William C. Dowlan and starring Alma Rubens, Kathryn Adams and Jack Conway.
