The Fortune Teller	1920	{"Marjorie Rambeau","Frederick Burton","Raymond McKee"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Fortune Teller is a lost 1920 American silent drama film directed by Albert Capellani and starring Marjorie Rambeau. It is based on a 1919 Broadway play, The Fortune Teller, by Leighton Graves Osmun. The film was distributed by Robertson-Cole Distributors.
