The Bronze Bell	1921	{"Courtenay Foote","John Davidson","Claire Du Brey"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Bronze Bell is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by James W. Horne and written by Del Andrews and Louis Stevens based upon a novel by Louis Joseph Vance. The film stars Courtenay Foote, Doris May, John Davidson, Claire Du Brey, Noble Johnson, Otto Hoffman, and Gerald Pring. The film was released on June 19, 1921, by Paramount Pictures.
Bucking the Line	1921	{"Maurice 'Lefty' Flynn","Molly Malone","Kathryn McGuire"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Bucking the Line is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by Carl Harbaugh and starring Maurice 'Lefty' Flynn, Molly Malone and Kathryn McGuire.
