Bunty Pulls the Strings	1921	{"Leatrice Joy","Russell Simpson","Raymond Hatton"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Bunty Pulls the Strings is a lost 1921 American silent comedy film directed by Reginald Barker and starring Leatrice Joy. It is based on a Broadway play by Graham Moffat. On stage the part of Bunty was played and made famous by Molly Pearson. The film was produced and distributed by Goldwyn Pictures.
Buried Treasure	1921	{"Marion Davies","Norman Kerry","Anders Randolf"}	{"Adventure","Silent"}	Buried Treasure is a 1921 American silent adventure film directed by George D. Baker and written by George D. Baker and F. Britten Austin. The film stars Marion Davies, Norman Kerry, Anders Randolf, Edith Shayne, Earl Schenck, John Charles, and Thomas Findley. The film was released on April 10, 1921, by Paramount Pictures.
Burn 'Em Up Barnes	1921	{"Johnny Hines","Edmund Breese","George Fawcett"}	{"Comedy","Action","Silent"}	Burn 'Em Up Barnes is a 1921 American silent comedy action film directed by George Beranger and starring Johnny Hines, Edmund Breese and George Fawcett. It was loosely remade as a 1934 film of the same title.
The Butterfly Girl	1921	{"Marjorie Daw","Fritzi Brunette","King Baggot"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Butterfly Girl is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by John Gorman and starring Marjorie Daw, Fritzi Brunette, and King Baggot.
The Call of the North	1921	{"Jack Holt","Madge Bellamy","Noah Beery"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Call of the North is a 1921 American silent drama film produced by Famous Players-Lasky and distributed by Paramount Pictures. It was directed by Joseph Henabery and stars Jack Holt. It is based on the 1903 novel The Conjuror's House: a Romance of the Free Forest by Stewart Edward White and its 1908 play adaptation The Call of the North by George Broadhurst starring Robert Edeson. This film is a remake of an earlier 1914 version directed by Cecil B. DeMille. It is not known whether the film currently survives.
Camille	1921	{"Alla Nazimova","Rudolph Valentino","Patsy Ruth Miller"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Camille is a 1921 American silent drama film starring Alla Nazimova as Marguerite and Rudolph Valentino as her lover, Armand. It is based on the play adaptation La Dame aux Camélias by Alexandre Dumas, fils, which was first published in French as a novel in 1848 and as a play in 1852. Camille is one of numerous screen adaptations of Dumas, fils' story. The film was set in 1920s Paris, whereas the original version took place in Paris in the 1840s. It had lavish Art Deco sets and Rudolph Valentino later married the film's art director, Natacha Rambova.
Cappy Ricks	1921	{"Thomas Meighan","Agnes Ayres","John St. Polis"}	{"Adventure","Silent"}	Cappy Ricks is a 1921 American silent adventure film directed by Tom Forman and written by Peter B. Kyne, Albert S. Le Vino, Edward E. Rose, and Waldemar Young. The film stars Thomas Meighan, Charles S. Abbe, Agnes Ayres, Hugh Cameron, John St. Polis, Paul Everton and Eugenie Woodward. The film was released on August 21, 1921, by Paramount Pictures. \nOn Broadway in the 1919 season, the play version starred William Courtenay and Tom Wise.
The Case of Becky	1921	{"Constance Binney","Montagu Love","Glenn Hunter"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Case of Becky is a 1921 American silent drama film based on a successful 1912 play written by David Belasco and Edward J. Locke, The Case of Becky. Belasco also produced the play, which starred his muse, Frances Starr.
The Cave Girl	1921	{"Teddie Gerard","Charles Meredith","Boris Karloff"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Cave Girl is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by Joseph J. Franz and featuring Teddie Gerard, Charles Meredith, Lillian Tucker and Boris Karloff in an early film role. The source for the William Parker screenplay was the stage play of the same name by George Middleton and Guy Bolton. The film's tagline was "A Romance of Silent Trails and Rushing Waters... A Drama of Youth Gone Wild... Enacted in the Yosemite Valley in the Middle of Winter.". The film is presumed lost.
A Certain Rich Man	1921	{"Carl Gantvoort","Claire Adams","Robert McKim"}	{"Drama","Silent","War"}	A Certain Rich Man is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by Howard Hickman and starring Carl Gantvoort, Claire Adams and Robert McKim.
Charge It	1921	{"Clara Kimball Young","Herbert Rawlinson","Betty Blythe"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Charge It is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by Harry Garson and starring Clara Kimball Young.
The Charm School	1921	{"Wallace Reid","Lila Lee","Adele Farrington"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	The Charm School is a lost 1921 American silent comedy film starring Wallace Reid. Produced by Famous Players-Lasky and distributed through Paramount Pictures this James Cruze directed film was based on a 1920 Broadway stage play and novel by Alice Duer Miller that starred veteran actress Minnie Dupree. It is currently a lost film. It was filmed on the campus of Pomona College in Claremont, California.
The Charming Deceiver	1921	{"Alice Calhoun","Charles Kent","Robert Gaillard"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Charming Deceiver is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by George L. Sargent and starring Alice Calhoun, Charles Kent and Robert Gaillard.
Cheated Hearts	1921	{"Herbert Rawlinson","Warner Baxter","Marjorie Daw"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Cheated Hearts is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by Hobart Henley and featuring Herbert Rawlinson, Warner Baxter, Marjorie Daw and Boris Karloff. The screenplay was written by Wallace Clifton, based on the novel Barry Gordon by William Farquar Payson. The film's tagline was "All the Exotic Glamour of the East Woven in a Livid Picture of Love". It was shot in Universal City, and is today considered a lost film.
Cheated Love	1921	{"Carmel Myers","Allan Forrest","John Davidson"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Cheated Love is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by King Baggot and starring Carmel Myers, George B. Williams and Allan Forrest.
The Cheater Reformed	1921	{"William Russell","Seena Owen","Sam De Grasse"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Cheater Reformed is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by Scott R. Dunlap and starring William Russell, Seena Owen and Sam De Grasse.
The Chicken in the Case	1921	{"Owen Moore","Teddy Sampson","Katherine Perry"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	The Chicken in the Case is a 1921 American silent comedy film directed by Victor Heerman and starring Owen Moore, Vivia Ogden and Teddy Sampson.
Chickens	1921	{"Douglas MacLean","Gladys George","Claire McDowell"}	{"Comedy","Drama","Silent"}	Chickens is a 1921 American silent comedy drama film directed by Jack Nelson and written by Agnes Christine Johnston based on the story "Yanconna Yillies" by Herschel S. Hall. The film stars Douglas MacLean, Gladys George, Claire McDowell, Charles Hill Mailes, Raymond Cannon, and Willis Marks. The film was released on February 13, 1921, by Paramount Pictures. It is not known whether the film currently survives.
The Child Thou Gavest Me	1921	{"Barbara Castleton","Adele Farrington","Winter Hall"}	{"Drama"}	The Child Thou Gavest Me is a 1921 American drama film directed by John M. Stahl and written by Chester L. Roberts. The film stars Barbara Castleton, Adele Farrington, Winter Hall, Lewis Stone, William Desmond, and Richard Headrick. The film was released on August 20, 1921, by Associated First National Pictures.
Chivalrous Charley	1921	{"Eugene O'Brien","George Fawcett","Huntley Gordon"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Chivalrous Charley is a 1921 American silent comedy film directed by Robert Ellis and starring Eugene O'Brien, George Fawcett and Nancy Deaver.
Cinderella of the Hills	1921	{"Barbara Bedford","Carl Miller","Clarence Wilson"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Cinderella of the Hills is a lost 1921 silent drama film directed by Howard M. Mitchell and starring Barbara Bedford and Barbara La Marr. It was produced and distributed by Fox Film Corporation.
The City of Silent Men	1921	{"Thomas Meighan","Lois Wilson","Kate Bruce"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The City of Silent Men is a lost 1921 American silent drama film produced by Famous Players-Lasky and distributed by Paramount Pictures. It was directed by Tom Forman and starred Thomas Meighan and Lois Wilson.
Clay Dollars	1921	{"Eugene O'Brien","Ruth Dwyer","Frank Currier"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Clay Dollars is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by George Archainbaud and starring Eugene O'Brien, Ruth Dwyer and Frank Currier. It was shot at studios in Fort Lee, New Jersey.
Closed Doors	1921	{"Alice Calhoun","Harry C. Browne"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Closed Doors is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by Gustav von Seyffertitz and starring Alice Calhoun and Harry C. Browne.
Coincidence	1921	{"Robert Harron","June Walker","Bradley Barker"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Coincidence is a 1921 American silent comedy film starring Robert Harron and June Walker. It was Harron's first starring role after signing a deal with Metro Pictures Corporation, as well as his last film; Harron died of a self-inflicted gunshot wound in September 1920 between completion of filming and the release. It was directed by Chester "Chet" Withey and written by Brian Hooker based on a story by Howard E. Morton. The cinematographer was Louis C. Bitzer.
Cold Steel	1921	{"J.P. McGowan","Kathleen Clifford","Stanhope Wheatcroft"}	{"Action","Silent"}	Cold Steel is a 1921 American silent action film directed by Sherwood MacDonald and starring J.P. McGowan, Kathleen Clifford and Stanhope Wheatcroft.
Colorado	1921	{"Frank Mayo","Charles Newton","Gloria Hope"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Colorado is a 1921 American silent Western film directed by B. Reeves Eason and starring Frank Mayo, Charles Newton and Gloria Hope.
Colorado Pluck	1921	{"William Russell","Margaret Livingston","George Fisher"}	{"Drama"}	Colorado Pluck is a 1921 drama film directed by Jules Furthman. The film is based on the novel The Taming of Angela by George Goodchild. It is not known whether the film currently survives.
Conceit	1921	{"William B. Davidson","Hedda Hopper","Charles K. Gerrard"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Conceit is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by Burton George, produced by Selznick Pictures, and released by Select Pictures. The film stars William B. Davidson and Mrs. De Wolf Hopper, who later became a gossip columnist using the name "Hedda Hopper".
The Concert	1921	{"Lewis Stone","Myrtle Stedman","Raymond Hatton"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	The Concert is a lost 1921 silent comedy film directed by Victor Schertzinger and starring Lewis Stone, Myrtle Stedman, Raymond Hatton and Mabel Julienne Scott. It was produced and distributed by Goldwyn Pictures. It was based upon the 1909 play of the same title by Hermann Bahr.
Conflict	1921	{"Priscilla Dean","Edward Connelly","Hector V. Sarno"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Conflict is 1921 American silent drama film directed by Stuart Paton and starring Priscilla Dean, Edward Connelly and Hector V. Sarno.
A Connecticut Yankee	1921	{"Harry Myers","Pauline Starke","Rosemary Theby"}	{"Adventure","Silent"}	A Connecticut Yankee in King Arthur's Court is a 1921 American silent film adaptation of Mark Twain's 1889 novel A Connecticut Yankee in King Arthur's Court. The film was produced by the Fox Film Corporation and directed by Emmett J. Flynn based on a screenplay by Bernard McConville. It is notable as the first film adaptation of Twain's novel and as the second film about time travel to the past.
The Conquering Power	1921	{"Rudolph Valentino","Alice Terry","Ralph Lewis"}	{"Romance","Drama","Silent"}	The Conquering Power (1921) is an American silent romantic drama directed by Rex Ingram and starring Rudolph Valentino, Alice Terry, and Ralph Lewis. The film was based on the 1833 novel Eugénie Grandet by Honoré de Balzac. Its sets were designed by Ralph Barton.
The Conquest of Canaan	1921	{"Thomas Meighan","Doris Kenyon","Diana Allen"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Conquest of Canaan is a 1921 American silent drama film produced by Famous Players-Lasky and distributed by Paramount Pictures. It starred Thomas Meighan and Doris Kenyon and was directed by Roy William Neill. It was filmed in Asheville, North Carolina. A previous version of the story was filmed in 1916 under the same title.
Courage	1921	{"Naomi Childers","Sam De Grasse","Adolphe Menjou"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Courage is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by Sidney Franklin and starring Naomi Childers, Sam De Grasse and Adolphe Menjou. It was distributed by First National Pictures.
Cousin Kate	1921	{"Alice Joyce","Gilbert Emery","Leslie Austin"}	{"Drama"}	Cousin Kate is a lost 1921 American drama film produced and released by the Vitagraph Company of America. It is based on a 1903 play by Hubert Henry Davies. On the Broadway stage Ethel Barrymore made the role of Kate Curtis her own and was identified with it for many years. This film version was directed by a relative of Barrymore's, Lucille McVey, who was the second wife of Barrymore's uncle Sidney Drew. Alice Joyce stars in this film version.
Crazy to Marry	1921	{"Fatty Arbuckle","Lila Lee","Edwin Stevens"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Crazy to Marry is a 1921 American silent comedy film directed by James Cruze and starring Fatty Arbuckle. Prints are held by Cinematheque Royale de Belgique, Brussels and Gosfilmofond, Russian State Archive, Moscow.
Crossing Trails	1921	{"Pete Morrison","Esther Ralston","Lew Meehan"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Crossing Trails is a 1921 American silent Western film directed by Clifford Smith and starring Pete Morrison, Esther Ralston and Lew Meehan.
