Devil Dog Dawson	1921	{"Jack Hoxie","Helene Rosson","Evelyn Selbie"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Devil Dog Dawson is a 1921 American silent Western film directed by Karl R. Coolidge and starring Jack Hoxie, Helene Rosson and Evelyn Selbie. It was produced by Unity Photoplays and released on the states-rights market by Arrow Film Corp.
The Devil	1921	{"George Arliss","Lucy Cotton","Sylvia Breamer"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Devil is a surviving 1921 silent drama film directed by James Young and starring stage actor George Arliss in a film version of his 1908 Broadway success of Ferenc Molnár's play, The Devil [1]. Long thought to be a lost film, a print was discovered in the 1990s and restored by the Library of Congress.
The Devil Within	1921	{"Dustin Farnum","Virginia Valli","Nigel De Brulier"}	{"Adventure","Silent"}	The Devil Within is a 1921 American silent adventure film directed by Bernard J. Durning and starring Dustin Farnum, Virginia Valli and Nigel De Brulier.
Devotion	1921	{"Hazel Dawn","Elmo Lincoln","Violet Palmer"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Devotion is a 1921 American silent drama film directed by Burton George and starring Hazel Dawn, Elmo Lincoln and Violet Palmer.
Diamonds Adrift	1921	{"Earle Williams","Beatrice Burnham","Otis Harlan"}	{"Comedy","Silent","Romance"}	Diamonds Adrift is a 1921 American silent romantic comedy film directed by Chester Bennett and starring Earle Williams, Beatrice Burnham and Otis Harlan.
Disraeli	1921	{"George Arliss","Florence Arliss","Reginald Denny"}	{"Biography","Drama","Historical","Silent"}	Disraeli (1921) is an American silent historical drama film directed by Henry Kolker and starring George Arliss. This film features Arliss's portrayal of Benjamin Disraeli. He had played the same role in the play Disraeli in 1911. Arliss also reprised this role in the 1929 sound film Disraeli.
