The Highest Bidder	1921	{"Madge Kennedy","Lionel Atwill","Vernon Steele"}	{"Drama"}	The Highest Bidder is a lost 1921 American drama film directed by Wallace Worsley and written by Lloyd Lonergan. It is based on the 1920 novel The Trap by Maximilian Foster. The film stars Madge Kennedy, Lionel Atwill, Vernon Steele, Ellen Cassidy, Zelda Sears and Joseph Brennan. The film was released on January 15, 1921, by Goldwyn Pictures.
The Highest Law	1921	{"Ralph Ince","Robert Agnew","Margaret Seddon"}	{"Drama","Historical","Silent"}	The Highest Law is a 1921 American silent historical drama film directed by Ralph Ince and starring Ince, Robert Agnew and Margaret Seddon.
Hills of Hate	1921	{"Jack Hoxie","Wilbur McGaugh","Evelyn Nelson"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Hills of Hate is a 1921 American silent Western film directed by Ben F. Wilson and starring Jack Hoxie, Wilbur McGaugh and Evelyn Nelson.
His Brother's Keeper	1921	{"Martha Mansfield","L. Rogers Lytton","Gretchen Hartman"}	{"Crime","Silent"}	His Brother's Keeper is a 1921 American silent crime film directed by Wilfrid North and starring Albert L. Barrett, Martha Mansfield and L. Rogers Lytton. It is now considered a lost film.
His Greatest Sacrifice	1921	{"William Farnum","Alice Fleming","Evelyn Greeley"}	{"Drama"}	His Greatest Sacrifice is a 1921 American drama film directed by J. Gordon Edwards and written by Paul Sloane. The film stars William Farnum, Alice Fleming, Lorna Volare, Evelyn Greeley, Frank Goldsmith and Charles Wellesley. The film was released on April 17, 1921, by Fox Film Corporation.
His Nibs	1921	{"Chic Sale","Colleen Moore","Joseph Dowling"}	{"Comedy"}	His Nibs is a 1921 American comedy film directed by Gregory La Cava and starring Chic Sale and Colleen Moore.
Hold Your Horses	1921	{"Tom Moore","Sylvia Ashton","Naomi Childers"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Hold Your Horses is a 1921 American silent comedy film directed by E. Mason Hopper and starring Tom Moore, Sylvia Ashton and Naomi Childers.
The Hole in the Wall	1921	{"Alice Lake","Allan Forrest","Frank Brownlee"}	{"Drama"}	(for a 1929 early talkie remake starring Edward G. Robinson and Claudette Colbert see --The Hole in the Wall.)\n
The Home Stretch	1921	{"Douglas MacLean","Beatrice Burnham","Margaret Livingston"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Home Stretch is a surviving 1921 American silent drama film directed by Jack Nelson and written by Louis Stevens. The film stars Douglas MacLean, Beatrice Burnham, Walt Whitman, Margaret Livingston, Wade Boteler, Mary Jane Irving, and Charles Hill Mailes. Its screenplay was written by Louis Stevens and is based upon the short story "When Johnny Comes Marching Home" by Charles Belmont Davis, which appeared in the October 1914 issue of Metropolitan Magazine. The film was released on April 24, 1921, by Paramount Pictures.
Home Stuff	1921	{"Viola Dana","Tom Gallery","Josephine Crowell"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Home Stuff is a 1921 American silent comedy film directed by Albert H. Kelley and starring Viola Dana, Tom Gallery and Josephine Crowell.
