Kazan	1921	{"Jane Novak","Ben Deeley","Edwin Wallock"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Kazan is a 1921 American silent Western film. Now lost, it was directed by Bertram Bracken and starring Jane Novak and Ben Deeley. It was produced by William N. Selig and distributed independently. The picture was based upon a novel by James Oliver Curwood. In 1949 it was remade as a sound film of the same title.
