Know Your Men	1921	{"Pearl White","Harry C. Browne","Wilfred Lytell"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Know Your Men is a 1921 American silent melodrama film produced and distributed by Fox Film Corporation, directed by Charles Giblyn, and starring Pearl White. It is now considered to be a lost film.
Ladies Must Live	1921	{"Betty Compson","Mahlon Hamilton","Leatrice Joy"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Ladies Must Live is a 1921 American silent societal drama film directed by George Loane Tucker and released by Paramount Pictures. It was the last directorial effort of George Loane Tucker and was released four months after his death. Betty Compson stars along with Leatrice Joy, John Gilbert and Mahlon Hamilton. It was one of the few instances where future husband and wife Joy and Gilbert appeared in the same film.
