Afraid to Fight	1922	{"Frank Mayo","Lillian Rich"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Afraid to Fight is a 1922 silent American drama film directed by William Worthington and written by Charles Sarver. The film stars Frank Mayo, Lillian Rich, Peggy Cartwright, Lydia Knott, W.S. McDunnough, and Tom McGuire. The film was released on July 24, 1922, by Universal Film Manufacturing Company.
Alias Julius Caesar	1922	{"Charles Ray","Barbara Bedford"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Alias Julius Caesar is a 1922 American silent comedy film directed by Charles Ray and written by Edward Withers. The film stars Charles Ray, Barbara Bedford, William Scott, Robert Fernandez, Fred Miller and Eddie Gribbon. The film was released in July 1922, by Associated First National Pictures.
The Altar Stairs	1922	{"Frank Mayo","Louise Lorraine"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Altar Stairs is a 1922 American silent drama film directed by Lambert Hillyer and featuring Frank Mayo, Louise Lorraine, Lawrence Hughes and Boris Karloff in an early role. The screenplay was written by Doris Schroeder, George Hively and George Randolph Chester, based on the novel of the same name by G. B. Lancaster. It is considered today a lost film.
