The Black Bag	1922	{"Herbert Rawlinson","Virginia Valli"}	{"Mystery","Silent"}	The Black Bag is a lost 1922 American silent mystery film directed by Stuart Paton and starring Herbert Rawlinson. It was produced and distributed by the Universal Film Manufacturing Company.
Blaze Away	1922	{"Guinn 'Big Boy' Williams","Molly Malone","Hal Wilson"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Blaze Away is a 1922 American silent Western film directed by William Hughes Curran and starring Guinn 'Big Boy' Williams, Molly Malone and Hal Wilson.
Blazing Arrows	1922	{"Lester Cuneo","Francelia Billington","Clark Comstock"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Blazing Arrows is a 1922 American silent Western film directed by Henry McCarty and starring Lester Cuneo, Francelia Billington and Clark Comstock.
A Blind Bargain	1922	{"Lon Chaney","Raymond McKee"}	{"Horror","Silent"}	A Blind Bargain is a 1922 American silent horror film starring Lon Chaney and Raymond McKee, released through Goldwyn Pictures. The film was directed by Wallace Worsley and is based on Barry Pain's 1897 novel The Octave of Claudius. Lon Chaney played a dual role in the film, as both Dr. Lamb and "the Ape Man", one of Chaney's few "true horror films". The claim that Wallace Beery appeared as an ape-man uncredited has never been proven, but does persist in many sources.
