The Desert Outlaw	1924	{"Buck Jones","Evelyn Brent"}	{"Western","Silent"}	The Desert Outlaw is a 1924 American silent Western film directed by Edmund Mortimer and starring Evelyn Brent. Prints of the film survive in the Czech Film Archive.
The Desert Sheik	1924	{"Wanda Hawley","Nigel Barrie"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Desert Sheik is a 1924 American silent drama film directed by Tom Terriss and starring Wanda Hawley, Nigel Barrie and Pedro de Cordoba. British star Stewart Rome also appears in a supporting role. The story is inspired by the 1898 novel The Tragedy of the Korosko by Arthur Conan Doyle.
