Discontented Husbands	1924	{"James Kirkwood","Cleo Madison"}	{"Drama","Silent","War"}	Discontented Husbands is a 1924 American silent drama film directed by Edward LeSaint and written by Evelyn Campbell that was released by Columbia Pictures. The film stars James Kirkwood, Cleo Madison, and Grace Darmond. The film was released on January 15, 1924.
The Dixie Handicap	1924	{"Claire Windsor","Lloyd Hughes"}	{"Sports","Drama","Silent"}	The Dixie Handicap is a 1924 American silent drama film directed by Reginald Barker. The film stars Claire Windsor, Lloyd Hughes, and Otis Harlan. It is written by Waldemar Young.
Don't Doubt Your Husband	1924	{"Viola Dana","Allan Forrest"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Don't Doubt Your Husband is a 1924 American silent comedy film directed by Harry Beaumont and starring Viola Dana, Allan Forrest and Winifred Bryson.
Dorothy Vernon of Haddon Hall	1924	{"Mary Pickford","Anders Randolf"}	{"Historical","Drama","Silent"}	Dorothy Vernon of Haddon Hall is a 1924 American silent historical drama film directed by Marshall Neilan and starring Mary Pickford. The script by Waldemar Young was based upon the 1902 novel Dorothy Vernon of Haddon Hall by Charles Major.
The Dramatic Life of Abraham Lincoln	1924	{"George A. Billings","Ruth Clifford"}	{"Biography"}	The Dramatic Life of Abraham Lincoln is a 1924 American feature film directed by Phil Rosen and written by Frances Marion. By the date of release, the film's title was shortened to Abraham Lincoln, since the previous title was regarded as cumbersome.
Dynamite Dan	1924	{"Frank Rice","Boris Karloff"}	{"Action","Drama"}	Dynamite Dan is a 1924 American drama film directed by Bruce M. Mitchell and featuring Kenneth MacDonald and Boris Karloff. The film is about a young dockworker who is framed for a robbery he did not commit by his foreman, gangster Tony Garcia. Prints of this film survive and are available on DVD. Boris Karloff, who plays the gangster, only appears in the beginning and end of the film.
Dynamite Smith	1924	{"Jacqueline Logan","Bessie Love","Wallace Beery"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Dynamite Smith is a 1924 American silent drama film directed by Ralph Ince and written by C. Gardner Sullivan. The film stars Charles Ray, Bessie Love, and Wallace Beery, and was distributed through Pathé Exchange.
The Eagle's Claw	1924	{"Guinn \\"Big Boy\\" Williams","Lew Meehan"}	{"Western","Silent"}	The Eagle's Claw is a 1924 American silent Western film starring Guinn "Big Boy" Williams. It was produced and directed by Charles R. Seeling.
East of Broadway	1924	{"Owen Moore","Marguerite De La Motte"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	East of Broadway is a 1924 American silent comedy film directed by William K. Howard and starring Owen Moore, Marguerite De La Motte, and Mary Carr.
Empty Hands	1924	{"Jack Holt","Norma Shearer"}	{"Romance","Drama","Silent"}	Empty Hands is a 1924 American silent romantic drama film directed by Victor Fleming, and starring Jack Holt and Norma Shearer. The film was produced by the Famous Players-Lasky and distributed by Paramount Pictures.
Empty Hearts	1924	{"John Bowers","Clara Bow"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Empty Hearts is a 1924 American silent drama film directed by Alfred Santell. Adele Buffington wrote the scenario based on Evelyn Campbell's story published in Metropolitan.
The Enchanted Cottage	1924	{"Richard Barthelmess","May McAvoy"}	{"Romance","Drama","Silent"}	The Enchanted Cottage is a 1924 American silent drama film directed by John S. Robertson based upon a 1923 play by Arthur Wing Pinero.
The Enemy Sex	1924	{"Betty Compson","Percy Marmont"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Enemy Sex is a 1924 American silent drama film starring Betty Compson and directed by her husband James Cruze. It was produced by Famous Players-Lasky and released by Paramount Pictures. It is taken from the 1914 novel The Salamander by Owen Johnson.
Excitement	1924	{"Laura La Plante","Guy Edward Hearn"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Excitement is a 1924 American silent comedy film directed by Robert F. Hill and starring Laura La Plante. It was produced and distributed by Universal Pictures.
Fair Week	1924	{"Walter Hiers","Carmen Phillips"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Fair Week is a 1924 American silent comedy film directed by Rob Wagner and written by Thomas J. Geraghty and Walter Woods. The film stars Walter Hiers, Constance Wilson, Carmen Phillips, J. Farrell MacDonald, Bobbie Mack, and Mary Jane Irving. The film was released on March 16, 1924, by Paramount Pictures.
The Family Secret	1924	{"Baby Peggy","Gladys Hulette"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Family Secret is a 1924 American silent drama film directed by William A. Seiter and featuring child star Baby Peggy. It is based on Editha's Burglar, a story by Frances Hodgson Burnett first published in 1881 by St. Nicholas Magazine and adapted for the stage by Augustus E. Thomas.
Fast and Fearless	1924	{"Jay Wilsey","Jean Arthur"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Fast and Fearless is a 1924 American silent Western film directed by Richard Thorpe, written by Betty Burbridge and starring Buffalo Bill, Jr. and Jean Arthur. The film is mostly lost: only reel 2 out of 5 has been saved at the Library of Congress.
The Fast Set	1924	{"Betty Compson","Adolphe Menjou"}	{"Comedy","Drama","Silent"}	The Fast Set is a 1924 American silent comedy-drama film directed by William C. deMille and starring Betty Compson. The film is based on the 1923 Broadway play, Spring Cleaning, by Frederick Lonsdale.
The Fast Worker	1924	{"Reginald Denny","Laura La Plante"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	The Fast Worker is a 1924 American silent comedy film directed by William A. Seiter and starring Reginald Denny, Laura La Plante, and Ethel Grey Terry.
