Man of the Forest	1926	{"Jack Holt","Georgia Hale"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Man of the Forest is a 1926 American silent Western film directed by John Waters and written by Zane Grey, Max Marcin and Fred Myton. The film stars Jack Holt, Georgia Hale, El Brendel, Warner Oland, Tom Kennedy, George Fawcett and Ivan Christy. The film was released on December 27, 1926, by Paramount Pictures.
The Man Upstairs	1926	{"Monte Blue","Dorothy Devore"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	The Man Upstairs is a 1926 American silent comedy film directed by Roy Del Ruth and starring Monte Blue. It was produced and distributed by Warner Brothers. The film is based on the 1916 novel The Agony Column by Earl Derr Biggers.
Mantrap	1926	{"Clara Bow","Percy Marmont","Ernest Torrence"}	{"Romance","Comedy","Silent"}	Mantrap is a 1926 American silent comedy film based on the novel of the same name by Sinclair Lewis. Mantrap stars Clara Bow, Percy Marmont, Ernest Torrence, Ford Sterling, and Eugene Pallette, and was directed by Victor Fleming.
The Man Upstairs	1926	{"Monte Blue","Dorothy Devore","Helen Dunbar"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	The Man Upstairs is a 1926 American silent comedy film directed by Roy Del Ruth and starring Monte Blue. It was produced and distributed by Warner Brothers. The film is based on the 1916 novel The Agony Column by Earl Derr Biggers.
Mare Nostrum	1926	{"Antonio Moreno","Alice Terry"}	{"Spy","Drama","Silent","War"}	Mare Nostrum is a 1926 American silent war drama film directed by Rex Ingram. It was the first production made by Ingram while in voluntary exile and stars Ingram's wife, Alice Terry. The film is set during World War I, and follows a Spanish merchant sailor who becomes involved with a German spy. It is based on the novel of the same name by Vicente Blasco Ibáñez. Long thought lost, the film has recently been re-discovered and restored.
The Marriage Clause	1926	{"Francis X. Bushman","Billie Dove","Warner Oland"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Marriage Clause is a 1926 silent film drama directed by Lois Weber and starring Francis X. Bushman and Billie Dove. It was produced and released by Universal Pictures. The film marked a return to directing for Weber, who had taken a break for a few years.
Marriage License?	1926	{"Alma Rubens","Walter McGrail","Walter Pidgeon"}	{"Drama"}	Marriage License? is a 1926 American drama film directed by Frank Borzage and written by Bradley King and Elizabeth Pickett Chevalier. It is based on the 1925 play The Pelican by F. Tennyson Jesse and H. M. Harwood. The film stars Alma Rubens, Walter McGrail, Richard Walling, Walter Pidgeon, Charles Lane and Emily Fitzroy. The film was released on September 5, 1926, by Fox Film Corporation.
The Masquerade Bandit	1926	{"Tom Tyler","Dorothy Dunbar","Ethan Laidlaw"}	{"Action","Silent","Western"}	The Masquerade Bandit is a 1926 American silent Western film directed by Robert De Lacey and starring Tom Tyler, Dorothy Dunbar and Ethan Laidlaw.
Meet the Prince	1926	{"Joseph Schildkraut","Marguerite De La Motte"}	{"Comedy","Drama","Silent"}	Meet the Prince is a lost 1926 American comedy-drama silent film directed by Joseph Henabery and starring Joseph Schildkraut and Marguerite De La Motte. It was produced by Metropolitan Pictures Corporation and distributed by Producers Distributing Corporation.
