The Prince of Pilsen	1926	{"Anita Stewart","Allan Forrest"}	{"Comedy","Silent","War","Romance"}	The Prince of Pilsen is a lost 1926 American silent romantic comedy film directed by Paul Powell and starring Anita Stewart and George Sidney. David Belasco produced the film. It was based on a 1903 Broadway musical, The Prince of Pilsen, by Gustav Luders.
