Silken Shackles	1926	{"Irene Rich","Huntley Gordon","Victor Varconi"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Silken Shackles is a 1926 American silent drama film produced and distributed by Warner Bros. The film was directed by Walter Morosco, the son of theater owner Oliver Morosco, and based on a play by Charles Harris. Irene Rich leads the cast.
