Orchids and Ermine	1927	{"Colleen Moore","Jack Mulhall"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Orchids and Ermine is a 1927 silent film comedy starring Colleen Moore, filmed partly on location in New York. The film still exists. This was Mickey Rooney's first feature-length film.
Out All Night	1927	{"Reginald Denny","Marian Nixon"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Out All Night is a 1927 American silent comedy film directed by William A. Seiter and starring Reginald Denny, Marian Nixon and Wheeler Oakman.
