The Silver Slave	1927	{"Irene Rich","Audrey Ferris","Holmes Herbert"}	{"Drama","Silent","War"}	The Silver Slave is a lost 1927 silent film drama directed by Howard Bretherton and starring Irene Rich. It was produced and distributed by the Warner Brothers and a Vitaphone track of sound and effects was added, however there is no spoken dialogue.
Silver Valley	1927	{"Tom Mix","Dorothy Dwan"}	{"Action","Silent","Western"}	Silver Valley is a 1927 American silent Western film directed by Benjamin Stoloff and written by Harold B. Lipsitz and Malcolm Stuart Boylan. The film stars Tom Mix, Dorothy Dwan, Philo McCullough, Jocky Hoefli, Tom Kennedy, and Lon Poff. The film was released on October 2, 1927, by Fox Film Corporation.
Simple Sis	1927	{"Louise Fazenda","Clyde Cook","Myrna Loy"}	{"Comedy","Drama","Silent"}	Simple Sis is a 1927 American silent comedy-melodrama directed by Herman C. Raymaker and starring Louise Fazenda as a poor, plain laundress hoping for romance, supported by Clyde Cook as a shy suitor and Myrna Loy as a cruel beauty.
Sinews of Steel	1927	{"Alberta Vaughn","Gaston Glass","Anders Randolf"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Sinews of Steel is a 1927 American silent drama film directed by Frank O'Connor and starring Alberta Vaughn, Gaston Glass and Anders Randolf.
Singed	1927	{"Blanche Sweet","Warner Baxter"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	Singed is a 1927 American silent drama film produced and distributed by Fox Film Corporation. The film was directed by John Griffith Wray and stars Blanche Sweet. Singed is based on Adela Rogers St. Johns's story "Love o' Women".
The Siren	1927	{"Tom Moore","Dorothy Revier"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Siren is a 1927 American silent melodrama film directed by Byron Haskin. It stars Tom Moore, Dorothy Revier, and Norman Trevor, and was released on December 20, 1927.
Skedaddle Gold	1927	{"Hal Taliaferro","Bob Burns"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Skedaddle Gold is a 1927 American silent Western film directed by Richard Thorpe and starring Hal Taliaferro, Betty Baker and Bob Burns.
Slaves of Beauty	1927	{"Olive Tell","Holmes Herbert","Earle Foxe"}	{"Comedy","Drama","Silent"}	Slaves of Beauty is a 1927 American silent comedy drama film directed by John G. Blystone and starring Olive Tell, Holmes Herbert, Earle Foxe, Margaret Livingston, and future talent agent Sue Carol. The film was written by William M. Conselman from a story by Nina Wilcox Putnam entitled "The Grandflapper," edited by Margaret Clancey and photographed by L. William O'Connell, with intertitles by James Kevin McGuinness. The movie, released by the Fox Film Corporation, is a comedic send-up of the beauty salon industry with a running time of 60 minutes.
Slide, Kelly, Slide	1927	{"William Haines","Sally O'Neil"}	{"Comedy","War"}	Slide, Kelly, Slide is a 1927 American comedy film, released by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, directed by Edward Sedgwick, and starring William Haines, Sally O'Neil, and Harry Carey.
Slightly Used	1927	{"May McAvoy","Conrad Nagel","Robert Agnew"}	{"Comedy"}	Slightly Used is a 1927 American comedy film directed by Archie Mayo and written by C. Graham Baker and Jack Jarmuth. The film stars May McAvoy, Conrad Nagel, Robert Agnew, Audrey Ferris, Anders Randolf and Eugenie Besserer. The film was released by Warner Bros. on September 3, 1927.
The Slingshot Kid	1927	{"Buzz Barton","Jean Fenwick"}	{"Western","Silent"}	The Slingshot Kid is a 1927 American silent Western film directed by Louis King and written by Oliver Drake. The film stars Buzz Barton, Frank Rice, Jean Fenwick, Buck Connors, Jay Morley, and Arnold Gray. The film was released on December 4, 1927, by Film Booking Offices of America.
The Small Bachelor	1927	{"Barbara Kent","George Beranger"}	{"Comedy"}	The Small Bachelor is a 1927 American comedy film directed by William A. Seiter and written by John B. Clymer, Rex Taylor and Walter Anthony. It is based on the 1927 novel The Small Bachelor by P. G. Wodehouse. The film stars Barbara Kent, George Beranger, and William Austin. The film was released on November 6, 1927, by Universal Pictures. Carl Laemmle was the film's presenter.
Smile, Brother, Smile	1927	{"Jack Mulhall","Dorothy Mackaill","Philo McCullough"}	{"Comedy"}	Smile, Brother, Smile is a 1927 American comedy film directed by John Francis Dillon, and written by Dwinelle Benthall, Rufus McCosh and Rex Taylor. The film stars Jack Mulhall, Dorothy Mackaill, Philo McCullough, E. J. Ratcliffe, Harry Dunkinson and Ernest Hilliard. The film was released on September 11, 1927, by First National Pictures.
Smiling Billy	1927	{"Billy Sullivan","Armida","Jimmy Aubrey"}	{"Action","Silent"}	Smiling Billy is a 1927 American silent action film directed by Duke Worne and starring Billy Sullivan, Armida and Jimmy Aubrey.
The Snarl of Hate	1927	{"Johnnie Walker","Mildred June","Jack Richardson"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Snarl of Hate is a 1927 American silent drama film directed by Noel M. Smith and starring Johnnie Walker, Mildred June and Jack Richardson.
Snowbound	1927	{"Betty Blythe","Robert Agnew"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Snowbound is a 1927 American silent comedy film produced and released by Tiffany Pictures and directed by Phil Goldstone. It stars Robert Agnew, Betty Blythe and Harold Goodwin. A copy of Snowbound is preserved at the Library of Congress.
The Soda Water Cowboy	1927	{"Hal Taliaferro","Slim Whitaker"}	{"Western","Silent"}	The Soda Water Cowboy is a 1927 American silent Western film. Directed by Richard Thorpe, the film stars Hal Taliaferro, Beryl Roberts, and J. P. Lockney. It was released on September 25, 1927.
Soft Cushions	1927	{"Douglas MacLean","Sue Carol"}	{"Comedy"}	Soft Cushions is a 1927 American comedy film directed by Edward F. Cline and featuring Boris Karloff. It is a comic take by actor and producer Douglas MacLean on the 1911 play Kismet and the 1920 silent film adaptation. It is listed as being lost by Arne Andersen's Lost Film Files website.
Somewhere in Sonora	1927	{"Ken Maynard","Kathleen Collins"}	{"Western","Silent"}	Somewhere in Sonora is a 1927 American silent Western film directed by Albert S. Rogell and written by Marion Jackson. It is based on the 1925 novel Somewhere South in Sonora by Will Levington Comfort. The film stars Ken Maynard, Kathleen Collins, Frank Leigh, Joseph Bennett, Charles Hill Mailes and Carl Stockdale. The film was released on April 3, 1927, by First National Pictures.
