The Tigress	1927	{"Jack Holt","Dorothy Revier"}	{"Drama","Silent"}	The Tigress is a 1927 American silent drama film directed by George B. Seitz. The film is currently believed to be lost film.
Tillie the Toiler	1927	{"Marion Davies","Matt Moore","George K. Arthur"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Tillie the Toiler is a 1927 American silent film comedy produced by Cosmopolitan Productions and released through Metro Goldwyn Mayer studios. It is based on Russ Westover's popular comic strip Tillie the Toiler. The film was directed by Hobart Henley and stars Marion Davies.
Time to Love	1927	{"Raymond Griffith","William Powell","Vera Voronina"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	Time to Love is a 1927 American silent comedy film directed by Frank Tuttle and starring Raymond Griffith, William Powell and Vera Voronina. It is currently considered a lost film.
The Tired Business Man	1927	{"Raymond Hitchcock","Dot Farley","Margaret Quimby"}	{"Comedy","Silent"}	The Tired Business Man is a 1927 American silent comedy film directed by Allen Dale and starring Raymond Hitchcock, Dot Farley and Margaret Quimby. It was produced and released by the independent studio Tiffany Pictures. The film's sets were designed by the art director George Sawley.
