We're in the Legion Now!	1936	{"Reginald Denny","Esther Ralston"}	{"Adventure","Comedy"}	We're in the Legion Now is a 1936 American adventure comedy film directed by Crane Wilbur and shot in Magnacolor. The film is also known as The Rest Cure, which was the title of the 1934 original J.D. Newsom story the film was based on.
