Renegade Girl	1946	{"Ann Savage","Alan Curtis","Jack Holt"}	{"Western"}	Renegade Girl is a 1946 American western film directed by William Berke and starring Ann Savage, Alan Curtis and Edward Brophy. It was one of a few movies made by the short-lived Affiliated Productions, and was released through Robert L. Lippert's Screen Guild Productions.
