Thieves Like Us	1974	{"Keith Carradine","Shelley Duvall","Louise Fletcher"}	{"Drama","Crime"}	Thieves Like Us is a 1974 American crime film, set in the United States of the 1930s. It was directed by Robert Altman and starred Keith Carradine and Shelley Duvall. The film was based on the novel of the same name by Edward Anderson, which also supplied source material for the 1948 film They Live by Night, directed by Nicholas Ray. The Altman film sticks much closer to the book. The supporting cast includes Louise Fletcher and Tom Skerritt.
Thomasine & Bushrod	1974	{"Max Julien","Vonetta McGee","George Murdock"}	{"Western"}	Thomasine & Bushrod is a 1974 Western film directed by Gordon Parks, Jr., written by and starring Max Julien and Vonetta McGee and was released by Columbia Pictures. The title song was written by Arthur Lee and performed by his band Love.
Three the Hard Way	1974	{"Fred Williamson","Jim Kelly","Jim Brown"}	{"Action"}	Three the Hard Way is a 1974 action blaxploitation film directed by Gordon Parks Jr., written by Eric Bercovici and Jerrold L. Ludwig and starring Fred Williamson, Jim Brown, and Jim Kelly.
Thunderbolt and Lightfoot	1974	{"Clint Eastwood","Jeff Bridges","George Kennedy","Geoffrey Lewis"}	{"Crime","Drama","Comedy"}	Thunderbolt and Lightfoot is a 1974 American crime comedy film written and directed by Michael Cimino and starring Clint Eastwood, Jeff Bridges, George Kennedy, and Geoffrey Lewis.
