Defiance	2008	{"Daniel Craig","Liev Schreiber","Jamie Bell","George MacKay","Alexa Davalos","Allan Corduner","Mark Feuerstein","Mia Wasikowska","Tomas Arana","Jacek Koman","Iben Hjejle","Mark Margolis","Jodhi May","Kate Fahy","Iddo Goldberg","Sam Spruell","Ravil Isyanov","Martin Hancock","Jonjo O'Neill","Rolandas Boravskis"}	{"War"}	Defiance is a 2008 American war film directed by Edward Zwick set during the occupation of Belarus by Nazi Germany. The screenplay by Clayton Frohman and Zwick was based on Nechama Tec's 1993 book Defiance: The Bielski Partisans, an account of the eponymous group led by Polish Jewish brothers who saved and recruited Jews in Belarus during the Second World War. The film stars Daniel Craig as Tuvia Bielski, Liev Schreiber as Zus Bielski, Jamie Bell as Asael Bielski, and George MacKay as Aron Bielski.
