Hyde Park on Hudson	2012	{"Bill Murray","Laura Linney","Olivia Williams","Samuel West","Olivia Colman","Elizabeth Wilson","Elizabeth Marvel","Eleanor Bron"}	{"Comedy","Drama","Historical"}	Hyde Park on Hudson is a 2012 British historical comedy-drama film directed by Roger Michell. The film stars Bill Murray as Franklin D. Roosevelt, Olivia Colman as Queen Elizabeth, and Laura Linney as Margaret "Daisy" Suckley, a cousin and childhood friend of the President. It was based on Suckley's private journals and diaries, discovered after her death, and fictionally dramatizes her close personal relationship with Roosevelt and the 1939 visit of King George VI and Queen Elizabeth to Roosevelt's country estate.
