Kick-Ass 2	2013	{"Aaron Johnson","Chloë Grace Moretz","Christopher Mintz-Plasse","John Leguizamo","Donald Faison","Robert Emms","Morris Chestnut","Lyndsy Fonseca","Lindy Booth","Jim Carrey","Clark Duke","Olga Kurkulina"}	{"Comedy","Superhero"}	Kick-Ass 2 is a 2013 black comedy superhero film written and directed by Jeff Wadlow, based on the graphic novels Book Two and Book Three of Kick-Ass: The Dave Lizewski Years by Mark Millar and John Romita, Jr., and serving as a sequel to 2010's Kick-Ass. It stars Aaron Taylor-Johnson, Christopher Mintz-Plasse, Chloë Grace Moretz, and Jim Carrey, with the former trio reprising their roles from the first film. The film follows Dave Lizewski / Kick-Ass (Taylor-Johnson), who joins a vigilante team called "Justice Forever", while Mindy Macready / Hit Girl (Moretz) attempts to live a normal life, and Chris D'Amico (Mintz-Plasse) taking up the mantle of The Motherfucker and forming a supervillain team to take revenge on Kick-Ass.
